{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792330337,"nonce":"fgi8S7RlnSZViJEZKsoSVz+GeiE=","title":"A function's optimised code depends on whether its callees were optimised before it","message":"A callee goes into the scratch module as its optimised body when its cell is filled and as its lowered body otherwise, and the inliner decides from what is there. The two can decide differently: an optimised callee carries the error arms of what it inlined (ArrayList$__setitem__$s0 with zb_list_unbox_tagged_f64's TypeError report: eight calls, refused as a dispatch at loop sites where the lowered body inlines), and is a different size. So the code a function runs at the baseline and at LLVM depends on which of its callees reached their compile first.\n\nThis blocks raising zypy's baseline threshold, which shortens first iterations broadly. NUC, 4 pinned cores, CI's figure, 7 interleaved reps, threshold 80 against 20 on main 7ac7d368: crypto 0.775, spectral-norm 0.830, chaos 0.906, float 0.911, raytrace 0.950, nbody 0.955, fft 0.959, SOR 0.967, LU 0.976; ai, deltablue, fannkuch, go, hexiom2, json, meteor, nqueens, telco unchanged. 3 cores: crypto 0.81, spectral 0.80, float 0.83, fft 0.85, chaos 0.89, meteor 0.91. On 4 pinned cores the scoreboard with 571cd3ff and threshold 80 is 12 faster, 10 slower, against 9 and 13 for 7ac7d368.\n\nBut richards' steady state is about 1.5x slower at 80 (2.7 against 1.8 ms an iteration, still at iteration 10): with callees compiled first, DeviceTask$fn, HandlerTask$fn and IdleTask$fn inline a different set (HandlerTaskRec$deviceInAdd$trusted, Task$waitTask, Task$hold in other combinations), grow past the dispatch's size limit (\"too large\" where 20 says \"callee with calls outside a loop\"), and HandlerTask$fn gains a loop. The threshold patch is a one-line config in zyntax_python/src/main.rs, honouring ZYNTAX_BASELINE_THRESHOLD.\n\nWanted: the inliner's decision and the inlined body independent of compile order, from the lowered body always or the optimised one always (the latter once the dispatch test stops counting a callee's cold arms, cab4f9d / 5200715).","files":null}]}